1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:10,367
This is NTSOne, from NTS Digital Solutions. One platform for
registrations, voting, orders, payments and bookkeeping.

2
00:00:10,867 --> 00:00:19,940
Running events, elections, orders and money across paper
forms, spreadsheets and notebooks is slow, and mistakes are
easy to make.

3
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:27,658
NTSOne gives your organization one private workspace, with a
dashboard that shows everything at a glance.

4
00:00:28,158 --> 00:00:37,201
Build registration forms with drag and drop, share a link or
a QR code, and issue ID cards and tickets that can be
checked at the door.

5
00:00:37,701 --> 00:00:44,259
Run secret-ballot elections, with optional paid votes and
live results that update as people vote.

6
00:00:44,759 --> 00:00:52,762
Give your business an online order page, and create
invoices, receipts, quotations and business cards in
minutes.

7
00:00:53,262 --> 00:01:01,496
Accept Orange Money, Africell Money and QMoney, and follow
every payment, refund and withdrawal in your payment fund.

8
00:01:01,996 --> 00:01:09,309
Keep simple books, track monthly contributions, and manage
wish lists, all in the same place.

9
00:01:09,809 --> 00:01:15,738
NTSOne. One platform. Endless possibilities.

10
00:01:14,460 --> 00:01:25,462
In this video you will learn how to get started with NTSOne. Create your account, sign
in, find your way around the dashboard, and manage your settings.

11
00:01:26,062 --> 00:01:40,325
Start on the NTSOne home page. It shows everything the platform can do, from
registrations and voting to orders, payments and bookkeeping. To begin, choose Get
started or Create your account.

12
00:01:40,925 --> 00:02:00,716
Enter your organization's name, your name, your email address, and a strong password,
then agree to the terms and press Create account. We email you a six character code.
Enter it to confirm your email address, and your workspace is ready. You can also sign
up with Google.

13
00:02:01,316 --> 00:02:12,169
Next time, sign in with your email and password. If you forget your password, choose
Forgot password, and we will email you a link to choose a new one.

14
00:02:12,769 --> 00:02:27,366
After you sign in, you land on your dashboard. It summarizes your programs and
registrations, then your voting polls, your businesses, your payments, and your books,
so you can see how everything is going at a glance.

15
00:02:27,966 --> 00:02:41,363
The menu on the left takes you to each part of NTSOne: Programs, Voting Polls,
Businesses, your Wish List, Contributions, Users, your Payment fund, and Settings.

16
00:02:41,963 --> 00:02:52,591
Use the moon button at the top to switch between light and dark mode. The round button
with your initials opens your profile menu, where you can open Settings or log out.

17
00:02:53,191 --> 00:03:05,833
In Settings you can change your name and photo, your organization's name, your email
address and your password. Any other organizations you belong to are listed there,
with a button to leave them.

18
00:03:06,433 --> 00:03:20,745
At the bottom of Settings you can delete your account. You need your password, and you
must type the word DELETE. If you are the only person in your organization, its data
is deleted too, so this cannot be undone.

19
00:03:21,345 --> 00:03:31,787
If you need help, use the Contact page, or the Send feedback button inside the app.
You can also report a concern from the footer of any public page.

20
00:03:32,387 --> 00:03:41,330
That is how to get started with NTSOne. Use this video as your guide, and watch the
next videos to learn each part in detail.

21
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:53,707
In this video you will learn how to run a registration from
start to finish with NTSOne. Create a program, build and
publish its form, collect registrations, and manage them.

22
00:03:54,307 --> 00:04:09,523
Open Programs and choose New Program. Give it a name and a
short description, then select Create program. Your program
starts as a draft, with tabs for its form, registrations,
analytics and verifications.

23
00:04:10,123 --> 00:04:25,791
Next, open the Form Builder. Choose a type of question, such
as Short Text, press Add field, and give it a label. You can
mark a question as required. There are twenty three question
types to choose from.

24
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:38,758
Add the rest of your questions: email, phone number, date of
birth, or a yes or no question. Use Preview to see exactly how
the form will look to the people who register.

25
00:04:39,358 --> 00:04:52,345
When you are happy with it, choose Save Draft, then Publish.
Then publish the program itself and open registration. Your
program now has a public link and a QR code that you can
share.

26
00:04:52,945 --> 00:05:04,453
This is what a registrant sees. If they miss a required
answer, the problem is shown right under that question, with a
red outline, so they know exactly what to fix.

27
00:05:05,053 --> 00:05:17,945
As they fill in the form, each answer turns green when it is
correct. After they submit, they receive a registration
number, and they can preview, print or download a copy of
their registration.

28
00:05:18,545 --> 00:05:34,716
Back in your workspace, the Registrations tab lists everyone
who has registered. You can search, filter by status or date,
import from Excel, and export to Excel or CSV. Open a
registration to read every answer.

29
00:05:35,316 --> 00:05:46,504
To update a registration, choose a new status, such as
Approved, add an optional note, and press Update status. Every
change is saved in the history.

30
00:05:47,104 --> 00:06:05,360
NTSOne can also issue ID cards and tickets with a QR code.
Turn them on from the program page, pick a design, and each
registrant gets their own. When a code is scanned at the door,
the Verifications tab records who it was, whether it was
valid, and when.

31
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:15,303
That is how you run a registration with NTSOne. Use this video
as your guide, and watch the next video to learn about voting
polls.

32
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:26,042
In this video you will learn how to run a voting poll with
NTSOne. Create a poll, build its ballot, open voting, and
watch the results arrive live.

33
00:06:26,642 --> 00:06:44,813
Open Voting Polls and choose New Poll. Give it a name and a
description. Then decide whether voters need an account. If
they do, they sign up and confirm their email. If not, anyone
with the link can vote straight away, and each browser counts
as one voter.

34
00:06:45,413 --> 00:06:58,236
Next, open the Ballot tab and add a position, such as
President. Add a candidate for each person on the ballot, with
an optional photo and short description. Then save the ballot.

35
00:06:58,836 --> 00:07:11,293
On the Overview tab you choose the rules. You can allow one
vote per email, show live results to voters, be emailed about
each vote, and decide whether voters must create an account.

36
00:07:11,893 --> 00:07:27,770
When everything is ready, press Open voting. You can also set
a time for the poll to close by itself. Voting can be free, or
you can ask voters to pay for their votes with the paid voting
settings, and agree to the platform fee first.

37
00:07:28,370 --> 00:07:41,992
This is what a voter sees. They open the link, choose one
candidate for each position, and press Vote. They are thanked
straight away, and if you allow it, the live results update as
people vote.

38
00:07:42,592 --> 00:07:53,815
When a poll asks for accounts, voters first sign in or create
an account. You can also limit voting to certain email
domains, or to a list of verified voters.

39
00:07:54,415 --> 00:08:07,392
The Results tab shows each candidate's votes, percentage and
place, and you can export them. The Voters tab shows who
voted, but never who they voted for, because the ballot stays
secret.

40
00:08:07,992 --> 00:08:17,050
That is how you run a voting poll with NTSOne. Use this video
as your guide, and watch the next video to learn about
businesses.

41
00:08:17,670 --> 00:08:29,252
In this video you will learn how to run a business with
NTSOne. Create a business, put your products online, take an
order from a customer, and send an invoice.

42
00:08:29,852 --> 00:08:48,963
Open Businesses and choose New Business. Enter its name,
email, phone, address and a short description. Your business
gets its own workspace, with tabs for the order form, orders,
quotations, invoices, receipts, business cards, bookkeeping
and analytics.

43
00:08:49,563 --> 00:09:04,655
Open the Order Form tab and add the items you sell, each with
a name and a price. You can also add pictures and videos. Then
add the questions customers must answer, such as their name,
phone number and delivery address.

44
00:09:05,255 --> 00:09:18,587
Save and publish the form, then choose Start taking orders.
Your order page now has its own link and a QR code, so
customers can open it from a message, a poster or a social
media post.

45
00:09:19,187 --> 00:09:30,390
This is your online shop. Customers see your business details,
browse your products, and add what they want to their order.
The total updates as they go.

46
00:09:30,990 --> 00:09:45,447
At checkout the customer enters their details, reviews the
order, and confirms it. When payments are turned on, they pay
with mobile money at this point. They then get an order number
and a copy of their order to keep.

47
00:09:46,047 --> 00:10:01,949
Back in your workspace, the Orders tab lists every order. Open
one to see the items, the customer's answers and its history.
Choose a new status, add a note, and update it, and the
customer can be emailed at each step.

48
00:10:02,549 --> 00:10:20,501
To bill a client, open Invoices and choose New invoice. Enter
the client, the items, quantities and prices. Save it, and you
can print it, download it as a PDF, or send it by email.
Receipts and quotations work the same way.

49
00:10:21,101 --> 00:10:32,008
The same tabs let you create receipts and quotations, design
business cards with a QR code, and follow your orders, money
invoiced and money received in Analytics.

50
00:10:32,608 --> 00:10:41,346
That is how you run a business with NTSOne. Use this video as
your guide, and watch the next video to learn about payments.

51
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:54,977
In this video you will learn how payments work in NTSOne: how to switch them on, how
the payment fund works, and how to withdraw your money. The amounts you will see are
sample demonstration data.

52
00:10:55,577 --> 00:11:11,239
Open a program, an order form or a poll, and find the Payments section. Switch on Take
payments and set what each thing costs, such as a registration fee. People then pay
with Orange Money, Africell Money or QMoney.

53
00:11:11,839 --> 00:11:32,175
The platform keeps a small fee from every payment, and an organization admin must
agree to it first. If you try to save without ticking the box, you are asked to agree.
Tick it and save, and payments are on. If you change a setting later, the box clears,
and you tick it again before saving.

54
00:11:32,775 --> 00:11:43,413
The Payments tab of the program lists every payment, who paid, how they paid, and its
status. Paid, cancelled and waiting payments are all recorded.

55
00:11:44,013 --> 00:12:01,880
All the money goes to your payment fund. Available is what you can withdraw now. On
hold is money still inside the short waiting time after a payment. Below, you can see
the total received all time, the total after the platform fee, and the total after
refunds.

56
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:24,026
To withdraw, first add a withdrawal account, a mobile money number or a bank account,
and confirm with your password. A new account can be used after a short waiting time.
Then press Withdraw, choose the account and the amount, and confirm with your
password. Large withdrawals wait for approval from the platform team.

57
00:12:24,626 --> 00:12:40,803
If you want your money sent on straight away, turn on Automatic withdrawal. Choose an
account and confirm with your password. From then on, each successful payment is sent
to that account with no waiting time, and the platform fee is still taken.

58
00:12:41,403 --> 00:12:53,631
Everything is recorded. The Withdrawals table shows each withdrawal and its status,
and Money in and out lists every payment received, every fee and every withdrawal,
newest first.

59
00:12:54,231 --> 00:13:12,892
The platform team sees every organization's totals: money paid in, fees, refunds,
withdrawals, and what is left in each fund. For each organization they can also set
the platform fee, the waiting time before money can be withdrawn, and when withdrawals
switch on.

60
00:13:13,492 --> 00:13:19,151
That is how payments work in NTSOne. Use this video as your guide.

61
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:34,391
In this video you will learn how to keep simple books for your business with NTSOne.
Write down sales, spending and loans, and see your profit and who owes what. The
amounts you will see are sample demonstration data.

62
00:13:34,991 --> 00:13:51,278
Open a business and choose Bookkeeping. My book shows your profit this month, the
money you have, what people owe you, and what you owe. Below are big buttons for
everything that can happen in a business. Nothing is ever deleted from your book.

63
00:13:51,878 --> 00:14:11,465
To record a sale, press I sold something. Enter how much, say whether it was paid now
or on credit, who bought it, what it was for, and how it was paid. Then press Write it
in the book. If the customer will pay later, choose On credit, and the book remembers
that they owe you.

64
00:14:12,065 --> 00:14:24,863
Do the same for money you spent, stock you bought, money you received, and money you
put in or took out. Your summary updates straight away, showing your profit and how
much people owe you.

65
00:14:25,463 --> 00:14:40,385
All entries lists everything written in the book, with the date, what it was, who it
was with, how it was paid, and how much is still not paid. You can search, filter by
date, and export to Excel or CSV.

66
00:14:40,985 --> 00:14:53,377
To record a loan, press I lent money or I borrowed money. Enter the person, the
amount, and when it should be paid back. The Loans tab then shows each loan and how
much is left to pay.

67
00:14:53,977 --> 00:15:07,950
Reports show your profit and loss, your cash flow, and who owes what, for this month,
last month, this year, or any dates you choose. You can export them, and the Listen
button reads a report aloud.

68
00:15:08,550 --> 00:15:19,992
If writing is hard, use Voice notes. Press the microphone, say what happened, and the
recording is kept in your book. You can write it into the book later.

69
00:15:20,592 --> 00:15:26,481
That is how you keep your books with NTSOne. Use this video as your guide.

70
00:15:27,070 --> 00:15:41,176
In this video you will learn two simple tools in NTSOne: Contributions, to track money
that a group collects, and Wish lists, to plan what you want to get. The names and
amounts shown are sample data.

71
00:15:41,776 --> 00:16:01,213
Open Contributions and choose New contribution. Give it a name and say what the money
is for. Choose Monthly, for dues that people pay every month, or One time. Add the
columns you want to keep for each contributor, such as their name and phone number,
and the expected monthly amount.

72
00:16:01,813 --> 00:16:12,630
Each contribution shows the money collected, the money taken out, and the money still
held. The Overview tab also shows the totals year by year and who is behind.

73
00:16:13,230 --> 00:16:34,846
The Monthly tracker has a row for every contributor and a column for every month. Paid
months are green, a month paid less than expected is orange, and a month not paid is
red. Click a month to record a payment. Once a month has passed, a recorded payment is
locked, but months that were never filled in can still be filled in later.

74
00:16:35,446 --> 00:16:52,892
The Contributors tab is where you add and edit the people. Money taken records every
amount the group takes out, with a note saying why, so the balance held is always
clear. History keeps a record of every change, and you can export any table to Excel
or CSV.

75
00:16:53,492 --> 00:17:08,959
Wish lists are private lists of things you want to buy or have. Choose New wish list,
give it a name, and optionally a budget and a target date. Then choose Add items, and
add what you wish for, one by one or many at once.

76
00:17:09,559 --> 00:17:29,049
Type each item with an optional quantity and price each, or paste a whole list. The
priority and category you choose apply to all the items you add together. You can edit
an item later to add more details. You can search the list, filter it by priority or
category, and sort it.

77
00:17:29,650 --> 00:17:48,866
When you get something, press Got it. Enter the total price you paid, the date you got
it, and where it came from, with an optional note. It moves to the Gotten tab, which
shows how much you saved compared with the price you expected, and the progress bar
shows how much of your budget is spent.

78
00:17:49,466 --> 00:18:03,843
The Summary tab shows your budget, and your items by category, by month and by
priority. The Activity tab is a record that cannot be changed. Nothing is ever
deleted: removed items stay in the records.

79
00:18:04,443 --> 00:18:21,744
You can share a list with family or friends. Choose Invite someone, and they get their
own private link and QR code. You decide whether they can only look, or also add and
change items. They do not need an account, and they can only see that one list.

80
00:18:22,344 --> 00:18:29,302
That is how you use contributions and wish lists in NTSOne. Use this video as your
guide.

81
00:18:29,910 --> 00:18:38,352
In this video you will learn how to build your team in NTSOne, give each person the
right access, and keep your account secure.

82
00:18:38,952 --> 00:18:54,225
Open Users to see your team. Each person has a name, an email address, a role and a
status. As an organization admin, you can search, filter by date, and export the list
to Excel or CSV.

83
00:18:54,825 --> 00:19:13,746
To add someone, choose Invite teammate. Enter their name and email address, and pick a
role: Viewer or Program admin. They receive an email with a link to accept the
invitation and choose their own password. If they already have an account, they are
simply added to your team.

84
00:19:14,346 --> 00:19:32,387
A viewer can only look at what they are given. A program admin can manage it. Only an
organization admin can manage the team, the payment fund, withdrawals and refunds, and
agree to the platform fee. You can change a person's role from this list at any time.

85
00:19:32,987 --> 00:19:49,604
Access is given item by item. Press the access button next to a person to see which
programs, voting polls and businesses they can open. Grant a new one with a role, or
remove it with the bin. Someone only ever sees what you have given them.

86
00:19:50,204 --> 00:20:03,141
This is what a viewer sees. Their dashboard and lists only show what they were given.
They can also start a space of their own, where they are the admin, without losing the
access they were invited to.

87
00:20:03,741 --> 00:20:17,508
People can always leave. In their Settings, other organizations they belong to are
listed, and pressing Leave removes their access to everything in that organization. An
owner cannot leave their own organization.

88
00:20:18,108 --> 00:20:34,909
Sign-in attempts are limited, so guessing passwords is slow. Passwords must be strong,
and you can change yours at any time in Settings. New accounts confirm their email
address with a code, and everything done in the system is recorded in the audit log.

89
00:20:35,509 --> 00:20:41,903
That is how you manage your team and keep your account secure. Use this video as your
guide.

90
00:20:42,520 --> 00:21:00,731
This video is for the platform team, the super admins who look after every
organization on NTSOne. You will see accounts, the inbox, payments, the platform fund,
maintenance, backups and the audit log. The data shown is demonstration data.

91
00:21:01,331 --> 00:21:14,814
A super admin has extra items in the menu: Accounts, Inbox, Payments, Platform fund,
Backup and Recovery, Maintenance and Audit log. These are only visible to the platform
team.

92
00:21:15,414 --> 00:21:39,114
Accounts lists every organization, its owner, and how many users, programs, polls and
businesses it has. Open one to see its users, which you can suspend or reactivate, and
its programs. Here you also set that organization's payment terms: the platform fee,
the waiting time before money can be withdrawn, and when withdrawals switch on.

93
00:21:39,714 --> 00:21:55,196
The inbox gathers everything people send to the platform team: feedback from inside
the app, messages from the contact form, and reports of concerns. Open a message to
read it, reply by email, and mark it resolved.

94
00:21:55,796 --> 00:22:15,067
The Payments page shows what every organization has been paid, the fees taken,
refunds, withdrawals and what is left in each fund. Below, you approve or decline
large withdrawals and refunds, and look at payments that need a check. A request can't
be approved by the person who made it.

95
00:22:15,667 --> 00:22:33,759
The platform fund is the platform's own money: the fees it keeps from every payment.
You can see the balance, add a withdrawal account, withdraw, and follow every fee in
Money in and out. In this demo, Monime is not connected, so withdrawing is switched
off.

96
00:22:34,359 --> 00:22:55,770
When you need to work on the system, turn on Maintenance mode. Write the message
people will see, give an expected time back, and choose to show a message at the top
of the page or replace the page. You can show it everywhere or only on some parts, and
email team members and voters once. The platform team is never locked out.

97
00:22:56,370 --> 00:23:16,041
A full, encrypted copy of the database is made every day and checked before it counts.
You can back up now, verify a backup, download it, or restore from it, and every
restore is recorded with a safety copy taken first. The retention settings decide how
long old backups are kept.

98
00:23:16,641 --> 00:23:33,793
The audit log records every action in the system, grouped by account: who did it, what
they did, when, and whether it worked. Search it, filter by date, result or person,
and export it. Records cannot be changed or removed.

99
00:23:34,393 --> 00:23:40,866
That is how the platform team looks after NTSOne. Use this video as your guide.
